 "notes": {
  "n1": {
   "fill": "orange",
   "text": "Hub mode (final = D1h-1)\n\nOne centred window: `akl.run` + a house-icon link to akl.dev (icon only), then seven whole-row project links (pixel icon · name · one serif line). Row 1 `factory` minimises the window into factory mode (so does the lat/long readout and `m`); only the word Factorio in its line links out.\n\nDescriptions are one line on desktop and wrap to two below 760px. No index, no status, no years. Fonts to be self-hosted (JetBrains Mono + Newsreader).",
   "w": 420,
   "x": 3520,
   "y": 0
  },
  "n2": {
   "fill": "teal",
   "text": "Factory mode\n\nWindow fades out, `journalctl -u factory -f` comes back bottom-centre with a ring of 6 lines, a small production readout top-right, and `fg` top-left to return.\n\nEvery visible event writes a line: biter raids, turret fire, wall repair, blueprint construction, train arrivals + signals, rocket countdown/launch/cargo pod, radar charting, research, belt jams, brownouts, spidertron patrols, car trips, storms.\n\nStart state by host: akl.run → hub; factory.akl.run (or #factory) → this state immediately, no hub flash (a tiny sync boot.js sets html.factory before first paint). Same build, two custom domains; % fg / m / readout still bring the hub back.",
   "w": 420,
   "x": 3520,
   "y": 360
  },
  "n3": {
   "fill": "gray",
   "text": "Engine (World.dc.html)\n\nOne shared child component painting a seeded pixel-art world on a canvas. Tweaks: mode, time (day/dusk/night/cycle), rain, zoom, seed, still (one pre-simulated frame — used by the option boards so they don't each run a live sim).\n\nClick the map to send the camera somewhere.",
   "w": 420,
   "x": 3520,
   "y": 720
  },
  "t1": {
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 3430,
   "text": "akl.run — final: hub (Main), factory mode (Factory), phone, shared engine (World)",
   "w": 240,
   "x": 0,
   "y": -300
  },
